# Prevent repeated-glyph and repeated-line artifacts

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical implementation notes describe domain-only evidence. The finite
acceptance below does not claim full sampling, rendering or quality testing.

Detect frozen contours, identical word rhythms, mechanical baselines, local
white noise, and configurations that leave the calibrated writer's envelope.

Current executable evidence now freezes seven independent variation-quality
axes spanning those five artifact risks plus the accepted ADR's correlation
retention and extreme-legibility checks. One caller-computed finding is required
per axis. Duplicate or omitted axes reject structurally, while detected
artifacts remain evidence and are reported in canonical axis order. Structural
completeness now also produces constructor-sealed evidence, and canonical
detected-artifact projection can be repeated from that proof without rescanning
axis coverage.

All 128 combinations of not-detected/detected findings require the sealed and
direct projections to agree without depending on input order.

Statistical detectors, thresholds, perceptual metrics, correlation models,
legibility criteria, sampling, rendering, and release policy remain open.

## Finite seven-axis repeat-artifact and conservative fallback contract

**Inputs:** one deterministic contextual stroke plan, the selected profile's
observed/authorized variation bounds, a repeated-glyph/word/line review
corpus, and caller-computed findings for all seven required quality axes.
**Outputs:** a complete ordered artifact report, `ReviewRequired` or a
proposed bounded variation setting. Structural completeness is not a quality
pass and does not prove a specific person's visual style.

**Seven independent axes:** `CalibratedEnvelope`, `CorrelationRetention`,
`ExtremeLegibility`, `FrozenContours`, `LocalWhiteNoise`,
`MechanicalBaselines`, and `WordRhythmRepetition`. Require exactly one
finding per axis and retain original evidence source IDs and measurement
method. Missing/duplicate axes refuse the report before quality conclusions;
a detected artifact remains detected evidence, not an automatic source edit.

**Finite corpus:** render the repeated body fragment `la la`, a second line
also containing `la la`, and the same glyph `a` once in a title role. Review
contour identity, interglyph advance, shared line drift, join rhythm,
cross-scale correlation and legibility at the declared extremes. A proposed
first-release threshold flags repeated identical contour hashes and identical
word-spacing sequences if both repeats have admitted distinct context and
calibrated variation; it does not randomly alter strokes merely to evade a
hash match.

**Worked example:** profile `student-A` admits body-height 2.5..3.5 mm and
shared line drift at most 0.2 mm. Both `la` words happen to use the identical
baseline trace and contour, so report `FrozenContours=ArtifactDetected` and
`WordRhythmRepetition=ArtifactDetected` with the two word identities. Other
axes are individually marked `ArtifactNotDetected` only if their evidence was
measured; an unmeasured axis is incomplete and cannot imply a pass. Candidate
repair changes only authorized shared line/glyph variation and requires a
fresh seven-axis report.

**Conservative fallback:** if personal variation parameters or evidence are
absent, emit exactly the admitted nonvaried stroke plan with a visible
`NoVariationEvidence` limitation, or refuse when even deterministic base
strokes are missing. Do not fabricate naturalness or silently add independent
pixel noise. Static output may remain readable but cannot be called
writer-fidelity verified from this fallback alone.

**Refusal example:** a proposed extra slant breaks the profile's maximum,
white-noise jitter destroys a join, or a title extreme becomes unreadable.
Each blocks the revised plan, preserves the last accepted parameters and
reports the offending axis; no automatic release after merely counting all
seven findings. A detector absent from the runtime must be labeled theoretical.

**Assumptions and limits:** the existing evidence domain enforces seven-axis
completeness and canonical detected-artifact projection across all 128
finding combinations. Statistical detectors, actual contour comparison,
legibility criteria, reliable correlations, rendering and release scoring
remain unimplemented. This report contract is not a visual realism test.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for the quality-axis vocabulary/completeness; theoretical
  for detector thresholds and variation repair, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** seven-class report, two-line repeat example, nonvariation
  fallback and out-of-envelope/legibility refusals.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** statistical detection, calibrated
  threshold fitting, actual visual review or safe rendered ink repair.
